      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-20T07:32:12Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): turning rides keep no sample closer than half the chord share\n\nprofile_offset and profile_offset_in bisect each chord toward a\nvertical tangent of the offset curve. The bisection left runs of\nsamples less than a micrometre apart, and dedup() removed only exact\nduplicates. The lathe posts wrote these runs as identical G01 blocks.\n\nA new thin step drops each sample closer than half the chord share to\nthe last kept sample. The two window ends always stay. Each kept\nsample is an exact point of the offset curve. A chord moves by at\nmost two gaps, so the ride stays within half of the user tolerance.\n\nThe four lathe post goldens lose only the duplicate and sub-gap\nblocks (516 lines removed, none added).\n\nFixes #2882\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
